WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
Your history shouldn't disappear into a folder.

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.141
Modus connects your reports, your questions, and the original evidence.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.694
Each satellite is a file.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.527
Select one to see its readings.

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:14.192
One click opens the original, with dates, units, and printed lab context.

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:21.231
Muse Spark extracts a structured draft, checks the proposed evidence, and reads the source again for possible missing rows.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.746
This is a genuine saved Muse draft, reopened offline.

00:00:24.886 --> 00:00:28.312
The warning stays visible: the scan still needs visual review.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.825
Here, a separate CSV is read locally.

00:00:30.965 --> 00:00:32.837
You review the fields before saving.

00:00:32.977 --> 00:00:36.548
Corrections create new versions; the original never changes.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.226
When did I last have blood pressure of one hundred?

00:00:39.366 --> 00:00:40.495
First, which number?

00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:41.643
Choose systolic.

00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:44.907
The latest recorded match is May fourth, twenty sixteen.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:49.312
Open the evidence: one hundred over seventy, exactly as recorded.

00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:51.328
This answer uses offline tools.

00:00:51.468 --> 00:00:53.298
It's a statement about your records.

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.468
Two dates matter.

00:00:54.608 --> 00:00:58.757
This result happened in twenty nineteen, but arrived in twenty twenty-six.

00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:01.436
That distinction changes what we could have known.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.167
Replay twenty twenty-five.

00:01:03.307 --> 00:01:05.856
With today's files, the old result appears.

00:01:05.996 --> 00:01:08.770
Switch to files available then, and it disappears.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.522
Earlier knowledge stays intact.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.794
Conflicting copies stay side by side.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:14.681
Two point five and two point nine.

00:01:14.821 --> 00:01:18.499
Both sources remain visible; Modus doesn't silently pick a winner.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:24.621
Choose records, inspect the summary, and export it with the sources and unresolved differences attached.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.461
Muse proposes; you approve.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:30.147
Only reviewed transactions write to the encrypted local store.

00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:33.624
Original files, versions, and both clocks stay connected.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.575
Questions use bounded tools and checked evidence.

00:01:36.715 --> 00:01:39.965
Models cannot execute commands or rewrite your history.

00:01:40.105 --> 00:01:43.786
The result is traceable recordkeeping, without medical advice.

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:44.968
Modus Records.

00:01:45.108 --> 00:01:46.054
Ask your history.

00:01:46.194 --> 00:01:47.193
See the original.

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:48.599
Keep every correction.
